      "file": "hospitals.html",
      "sector": "Healthcare",
      "subsector": "Hospital",
      "companies": 13,
      "accent": "#0F5C58",
      "hook": "How India’s private hospital chains turn a bed-day into profit: a 1.5-beds-per-thousand shortage, a contested fight over who sets the price, a 34,000-bed construction wave that dents margins first, and a market paying 25–40x EBITDA for mid-teens returns — with all 13 listed chains compared side by side.",
      "tags": [
        "Bed shortage",
        "Pricing & regulation",
        "New-bed J-curve",
        "Valuation premium"
      ],
      "published": "2026-10-05"
    },
    {
      "name": "Pharmaceuticals",
      "slug": "pharmaceuticals",
      "file": "pharmaceuticals.html",
      "sector": "Healthcare",
      "subsector": "Pharmaceuticals",
      "companies": 47,
      "accent": "#26306E",
      "hook": "Two industries under one name: a branded annuity at home and a generics treadmill in the US. How 47 listed drugmakers make money, why the gRevlimid cliff, CDMO and the GLP-1 land-grab are reshaping them, and why the market pays about 40x earnings.",
      "tags": [
        "US generics",
        "India branded",
        "CDMO & China+1",
        "GLP-1"
      ],
      "published": "2026-10-05"
    }
